        ],
        "segment_ids": [],
        "anchors": []
      },
      "eyebrow": "Learn",
      "title": "Read the evidence, not the shortcut",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "These illustrative objectives are not AWS defaults. The alternative recovered marker changes the data-loss comparison, not restoration time. Retain the timestamps, marker and readiness evidence for both conclusions.",
          "role": "example",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f1",
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f2",
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f3"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#tb4"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "A running service proves neither objective. A good result for one cannot substitute for the other.",
          "role": "misconception",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f1",
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f2",
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f3"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#tb5"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Spreadsheet syntax for this worksheet: start a formula with =. C2 means column C, row 2. Subtract times with -, multiply with *, and use parentheses to group operations. Times are fractions of a day, so =ROUND((D2-C2)*1440,0) returns whole restoration minutes; =ROUND((C2-F2)*1440,0) returns whole data-gap minutes. ROUND(value,0) rounds to a whole number.",
          "role": "example",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f1",
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f2",
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f3"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#tb4"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "IF(test,\"pass\",\"fail\") returns pass when the test is true and fail otherwise; <= means less than or equal to. Compare restoration minutes with H2 and data-gap minutes with K2 separately. For example, =IF(ROUND((D2-C2)*1440,0)<=H2,\"pass\",\"fail\") returns the RTO conclusion.",
          "role": "example",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f1",
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f2",
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f3"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#tb4"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Put literal text in double quotes and join text, cell values and calculated values with &: =A2&\": RTO=\"&ROUND((D2-C2)*1440,0)&\" minutes \"&IF(ROUND((D2-C2)*1440,0)<=H2,\"pass\",\"fail\"). Extend this row summary with \"; RPO=\" and the separately calculated gap and RPO conclusion. Build the second summary by changing row references from 2 to 3, then join the summaries with &\" | \"&. Keep the measurements calculated from timestamps, not copied from result columns.",
          "role": "example",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f1",
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f2",
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#f3"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.verify_restored_service_and_data_against_rto_rpo_in_an_isolated_rehearsal#tb4"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        }
      ]
    },
