        "public": {
          "prompt": "In Sheet1, enter one formula in M2 that records both independent recovery measurements and pass/fail conclusions for rows 2 and 3, in that order. Columns: A case_id, C disruption_start, D passing_readiness_at, E readiness_evidence, F latest_recovered_marker, H rto_minutes, K rpo_minutes. Times are same-day HH:MM in an isolated rehearsal; the supplied readiness evidence confirms D is when checks passed. Compute restoration minutes from C to D and data-gap minutes from F to C, rounded to whole minutes. Compare restoration <= H and gap <= K independently. Do not use precomputed result columns G, I, J or L. Exact output format for each row: <case_id>: RTO=<minutes> minutes <pass/fail>; RPO=<minutes> minutes <pass/fail>. Join the two row summaries with \" | \". The sheet interprets HH:MM values as fractions of a day; multiply each time difference by 1440 to convert to minutes. Use formulas referencing the supplied cells; do not type measured answers. Any supported formula that produces the specified rounded measurements and independent conclusions is acceptable.",
          "asset_ref": {
            "asset_id": "ds.recovery_objectives"
