        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Spreadsheet syntax for this worksheet: start a formula with =. C2 means column C, row 2. Subtract times with -, multiply with *, and use parentheses to group operations. Times are fractions of a day, so =ROUND((D2-C2)*1440,0) returns whole restoration minutes; =ROUND((C2-F2)*1440,0) returns whole data-gap minutes. ROUND(value,0) rounds to a whole number.",
          "role": "example",
